# List page layouts

Use layout shells from `@/components/layout`. UI only — do not change API/business logic.

## Which component

| Pattern | Component | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Title + search/toolbar + table (no filters) | `ListPage` | Organizations, Campus |
| **Separate** filter card + table card (Angular default) | `FilteredListPage` | Subjects, Grade Setup, Room Details |
| **Separate** filter card + custom body (no AG Grid) | `FilteredPage` | Exam Max Marks |

```tsx
import { ListPage, FilteredListPage, FilteredPage, TableContextHeader } from '@/components/layout'
```

## FilteredListPage — Angular separated cards (default)

Filter card and table card are separate with a gap. Enabled by default (`filtersSeparated`).

```tsx
<FilteredListPage
  title="Subject Master"
  showTable={Boolean(courseId)}
  tableHeader={
    <TableContextHeader title="Subjects List" info={<>{univ} · {course}</>} />
  }
  filters={/* selects */}
  rowData={rows}
  columnDefs={columnDefs}
  toolbar={{ searchPlaceholder: 'Search…' }}
  toolbarTrailing={<Button>Add</Button>}
/>
```

- `tableHeader` defaults to book icon + page title; pass `null` to hide; pass `TableContextHeader` for custom title + selected-filter info.
- Opt out only when needed: `filtersSeparated={false}`.

## ListPage — header + table only

```tsx
<ListPage
  title="Organizations"
  rowData={rows}
  columnDefs={columnDefs}
  pagination
  toolbar={{ searchPlaceholder: 'Search…' }}
  toolbarTrailing={<Button>New</Button>}
/>
```
